  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which K-252a may interact with Complement C5, through a series of molecular targets that are all modulated by Gerontoisoflavone A and Vitetrifolin D. These compounds appear to act as intermediaries in the pathway leading from K-252a to Complement C5, with Gerontoisoflavone A and Vitetrifolin D both targeting different kinases—CLK2 and OSR1—before ultimately influencing Complement C5. The scores for these paths are consistent, indicating a plausible biological relationship, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated. The presence of multiple independent pathways supports the hypothesis, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct involvement of K-252a in the regulation of Complement C5. The mechanism appears to involve kinase modulation, which could influence downstream signaling pathways, potentially affecting immune responses through the complement system.",
